      en: "Padang, located on the rugged west coast of Sumatra, is the proud capital of the Minangkabau people. The city is globally famous for its cuisine, especially 'Rendang,' which has been voted the most delicious dish in the world. The Minangkabau cultural heritage, with its unique matrilineal social structure and iconic 'Buffalo-Horn' roof architecture, is present throughout the city. Geographically, Padang sits in one of the most seismically active zones on Earth, near the Sunda Trench, making it prone to earthquakes and tsunamis. Despite these risks, Padang remains a bustling trade center and the main gateway to the world-class surfing paradises of the Mentawai Islands. Geography K10 — Tectonic Risks and Disaster Mitigation."
